{"title": "Sectional Mock #149 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The number of prime numbers between 40 to 90 is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["13", "11", "12", "14"], "options_hi": ["n(2n  -  1)", "n(n + 1)(n + 2)", "(n + 1)(2n  -  1)", "n<sup>3</sup>(n  -  1)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>At a countryside food fair, a merchant sells 12 kg of rice with a 15% festival discount. The marked price is &#8377;52 per kg, while the actual cost price is &#8377;45 per kg. Unknown to buyers, the merchant's weighing scale gives only 800 grams when it shows 1 kg. What is his actual profit percentage? (Round your answer to two decimal places.)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368;&#2339; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2326;&#2366;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; 15% &#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2380;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; 12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 52 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 45 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2370; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; 800 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? (&#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;)</p>", "options_en": ["24.45%", "28.88%", "22.77%", "26.67%"], "options_hi": ["24.45%", "28.88%", "22.77%", "26.67%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>C.P = Rs. 45, M.P = Rs. 52</p><p>Actual C.P = 45 * 800/1000 = Rs. 36</p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 = 52 * 85/100 = Rs. 44.2</p><p>Profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>= (44.2  -  36) * 100/36</p><p>= 22.77%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>C.P = Rs. 45, M.P = Rs. 52</p><p>Actual C.P = 45 * 800/1000 = Rs. 36</p><p>S.P = M.P * (100  -  Discount)/100 = 52 * 85/100 = Rs. 44.2</p><p>Profit = (S.P  -  C.P) * 100/C.P</p><p>= (44.2  -  36) * 100/36</p><p>= 22.77%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Rajesh, in his printing press, got an order to print some books, out of which he completed 17/27 of the order in 34 days. In how many days, did he complete the entire order of printing?</p><p>Options:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2321;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2321;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; 17/27 &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; 34 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2331;&#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2321;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p><p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:", "options_en": ["60", "20", "54", "56"], "options_hi": ["60", "20", "54", "56"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Time taken to print 17/27 of the order to print some books = 34 days</p><p>Time taken to print the entire order to print the books = 34 *27/17 = 54 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Time taken to print 17/27 of the order to print some books = 34 days</p><p>Time taken to print the entire order to print the books = 34 *27/17 = 54 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the data carefully and answer the following questions. The following pie chart shows the total number of students in five different classes of the school. </p><p><img width=479 height=267 id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22866/image006.png\"></p><p>Find the total number of students in class X is what percent more/less than the total number of students in class VI. Total number of students in all five classes of school together is 32700. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2306;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"479\" height=\"267\" id=\"Picture 3\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22866/image006.png\"></p><p>&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; X &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; VI &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;/&#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 32700 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["120% less", "20% more", "120% more", "20% less"], "options_hi": ["120% &#2325;&#2350;", "20% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;", "120% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;", "20% &#2325;&#2350;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total percentage of students in class X =30% </p><p>Total percentage of students in class VI = 25%</p><p>Required percentage more/less = (30  -  25) * 100/ 25 = 20% more</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total percentage of students in class X =30% </p><p>Total percentage of students in class VI = 25%</p><p>Required percentage more/less = (30  -  25) * 100/ 25 = 20% more</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the unit's digit of the product 61*62*63*.........69</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; 61*62*63*.........69 &#2325;&#2366; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;</p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "0"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>If we observe carefully, the unit digit will be the result of the product of the unit digits of 61, 62,.........69</p><p>i.e., 1*2*3*4*5*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 2*5*1*3*4*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 10*1*3*4*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If we observe carefully, the unit digit will be the result of the product of the unit digits of 61, 62,.........69</p><p>i.e., 1*2*3*4*5*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 2*5*1*3*4*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 10*1*3*4*6*7*8*9</p><p>i.e., 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of the following expression?</p><p>112  -  76 + 13 x 7  -  128 &div; 16  -  45 x 2 </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>112 - 76 + 13 x 7 - 128 &div; 16 - 45 x 2</p>", "options_en": ["45", "29", "60", "20"], "options_hi": ["45", "29", "60", "20"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>We have:</p><p>112  -  76 + 13 x 7  -  128 &div; 16  -  45 x 2 </p><p>= 112  -  76 + 91  -  8  -  90</p><p>= 29</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We have:</p><p>112  -  76 + 13 x 7  -  128 &div; 16  -  45 x 2 </p><p>= 112  -  76 + 91  -  8  -  90</p><p>= 29</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>One decimal is 2.509 more than another decimal. If smaller decimal is 1.048, then find the larger decimal.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2375; 2.509 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; 1.048 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3.775", "3.585", "3.557", "3.675"], "options_hi": ["3.775", "3.585", "3.557", "3.675"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Smaller decimal = 1.048</p><p>Larger decimal = 1.048 + 2.509 = 3.557</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Smaller decimal = 1.048</p><p>Larger decimal = 1.048 + 2.509 = 3.557</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a seminar of 120 participants, 85 attended the morning session, 70 attended the afternoon session, and 20 attended neither. How many attended both sessions?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>120 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 85 &#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, 70 &#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2346;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; 20 &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2368; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["50", "55", "45", "40"], "options_hi": ["50", "55", "45", "40"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of participants attended at least one session = 120  -  20 = 100</p><p>Let A denotes the set of participants attended the morning session.</p><p>And B denotes the set of participants attended the evening session.</p><p>Using the formula,</p><p>n(A <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B) = n(A) + n(B)  -  n(A &#8745; B)</p><p>100 = 85 + 70 - n(A &#8745; B)</p><p>n(A &#8745; B) = 155  -  100</p><p>n(A &#8745; B) = 55</p><p>55 participants attended both sessions.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of participants attended at least one session = 120  -  20 = 100</p><p>Let A denotes the set of participants attended the morning session.</p><p>And B denotes the set of participants attended the evening session.</p><p>Using the formula,</p><p>n(A <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B) = n(A) + n(B)  -  n(A &#8745; B)</p><p>100 = 85 + 70 - n(A &#8745; B)</p><p>n(A &#8745; B) = 155  -  100</p><p>n(A &#8745; B) = 55</p><p>55 participants attended both sessions.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 20% people do not like any cold drinks and 640 people like Sprite, then how many people do not like any cold drink?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 20% &#2354;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 640 &#2354;&#2379;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379;&#2354;&#2381;&#2337; &#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2360;&#2306;&#2342; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["1000", "1200", "1500", "Other than above"], "options_hi": ["1000", "1200", "1500", "&#2313;&#2346;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let total population of village be P</p><p>20% people do not like any cold drink.</p><p>Number of people like sprite = 0.8 x 0.16P</p><p>(0.8 x 0.16) P = 640</p><p>P = (640000)/(16x 8)</p><p>= 5000</p><p>Number of people who do not like any cold drink = 0.2 x 5000 = 1000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total population of village be P</p><p>20% people do not like any cold drink.</p><p>Number of people like sprite = 0.8 x 0.16P</p><p>(0.8 x 0.16) P = 640</p><p>P = (640000)/(16x 8)</p><p>= 5000</p><p>Number of people who do not like any cold drink = 0.2 x 5000 = 1000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">14356", "q_hi": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">14356", "options_en": ["1/3", "3/5", "2/5", "3/4"], "options_hi": ["1/3", "3/5", "2/5", "3/4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The difference between 38% of a number and 24% of the same number is 135.10. What is 60% of that number</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 38% &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 24% &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 135.10 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 60% &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["588", "579", "610", "629"], "options_hi": ["588", "579", "610", "629"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>38% - 24% of number = 135.10</p><p>14% of number = 135.10</p><p>60% of number = 135.1 x 60/14 = 579</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>38% - 24% of number = 135.10</p><p>14% of number = 135.10</p><p>60% of number = 135.1 x 60/14 = 579</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>1/11<sup>th</sup> part of a pole is painted black, 1/2<sup>nd</sup> part of the rest is painted red and remaining 8.5m is painted white. What is the length of the pole?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; 1/11 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; 1/2 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 8.5 m &#2360;&#2347;&#2375;&#2342; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["18.7 m", "22.3 m", "16.2 m", "19.1 m"], "options_hi": ["18.7 m", "22.3 m", "16.2 m", "19.1 m"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>If the length of the pole is X cm, then,</p><p>(17/2) = X * (1  -  (1/11)) * (1  -  (1/2))</p><p>17/2 = X * (10/11) * (1/2)</p><p>X = 187/10 = 18.7 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If the length of the pole is X cm, then,</p><p>(17/2) = X * (1  -  (1/11)) * (1  -  (1/2))</p><p>17/2 = X * (10/11) * (1/2)</p><p>X = 187/10 = 18.7 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Study the given bar-graph and answer the question that follows.</p><p>The bar-graph shows the sales of books (in thousands) from six branches (B1, B2, B3, B4, B5 and B6) of a publishing company during two consecutive years 2000 and 2001.</p><p><img width=461 height=272 id=\"Chart 14\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27409/image027.png\"></p><p>The average sales of branches B1, B3 and B6 in 2000 is what percent of the average sales of branches B1, B2 and B3 in 2001?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;-&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>&#2348;&#2366;&#2352;-&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2342;&#2379; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; 2000 &#2324;&#2352; 2001 &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2358;&#2344; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2361; &#2358;&#2366;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; (B1, B2, B3, B4, B5 &#2324;&#2352; B6) &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2361;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=461 height=272 id=\"Chart 14\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27409/image027.png\"></p><p>2000 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; B1, B3 &#2324;&#2352; B6 &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; 2001 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; B1, B2 &#2324;&#2352; B3 &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["65.25%", "87.5%", "80.25%", "78.5%"], "options_hi": ["65.25%", "87.5%", "80.25%", "78.5%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Total sales of books from branches B1, B3 and B6 together in 2000 = 80 + 95 + 70 = 245000</p><p>average = 245000/3</p><p>total sales of books from branches B1, B2 and B3 in 2001 = 105 + 65 + 110 = 280000</p><p>average = 280000/3</p><p>required percentage = (245000/3)/(280000/3) * 100 &#8776; 87.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total sales of books from branches B1, B3 and B6 together in 2000 = 80 + 95 + 70 = 245000</p><p>average = 245000/3</p><p>total sales of books from branches B1, B2 and B3 in 2001 = 105 + 65 + 110 = 280000</p><p>average = 280000/3</p><p>required percentage = (245000/3)/(280000/3) * 100 &#8776; 87.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the difference between the sum of prime numbers between 30 and 40 to the sum of prime number between 40 and 50?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["64", "65", "63", "61"], "options_hi": ["n(2n  -  1)", "n(n + 1)(n + 2)", "(n + 1)(2n  -  1)", "n<sup>3</sup>(n  -  1)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the market price of a bag is 25% above the cost price, and a discount of 18% is declared on it, then find the gain percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2348;&#2376;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2366;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;, &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; 25% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360; &#2346;&#2352; 18% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2328;&#2379;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["1.5%", "2.0%", "3.0%", "2.5%"], "options_hi": ["1.5%", "2.0%", "3.0%", "2.5%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the cost price = Rs. 100</p><p>Marked price = 100 * 125/100 = Rs. 125</p><p>Selling price = 125 * 82/100 = Rs. 102.5</p><p>Gain percentage = (102.5  -  100)/100 * 100 = 2.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the cost price = Rs. 100</p><p>Marked price = 100 * 125/100 = Rs. 125</p><p>Selling price = 125 * 82/100 = Rs. 102.5</p><p>Gain percentage = (102.5  -  100)/100 * 100 = 2.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the number of trailing zeros in 1024! .</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1024 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;!</p>", "options_en": ["251", "253", "255", "257"], "options_hi": ["251", "253", "255", "257"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of trailing zeros in n! = highest power of 5 in n!</p><p>According to question,</p><p>1024/5<sup>1</sup> + 1024/5<sup>2</sup> + 1024/5<sup>3</sup> + 1024/5<sup>4</sup></p><p>= 204 + 40 + 8 + 1</p><p>= 253</p><p>Hence, number of trailing zeros is 253.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of trailing zeros in n! = highest power of 5 in n!</p><p>According to question,</p><p>1024/5<sup>1</sup> + 1024/5<sup>2</sup> + 1024/5<sup>3</sup> + 1024/5<sup>4</sup></p><p>= 204 + 40 + 8 + 1</p><p>= 253</p><p>Hence, number of trailing zeros is 253.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The table given below shows the number of officers working in six companies.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Companies</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Officers</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">400</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">500</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">F</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">600</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">G</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">350</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">H</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">450</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">I</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">800</td></tr></table><p>What is the total number of officers working in all the companies?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2331;&#2361; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2352;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">400</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">500</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">F</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">600</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">G</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">350</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">H</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">450</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">I</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">800</td></tr></table><p>&#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2352;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2900", "2600", "3400", "3100"], "options_hi": ["2900", "2600", "3400", "3100"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of officers = 400 + 500 + 600 + 350 + 450 + 800 = 3100</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of officers = 400 + 500 + 600 + 350 + 450 + 800 = 3100</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A = 4<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + .... + 44<sup>3 </sup>and B = 12<sup>2</sup> + 18<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup> + .... + 54<sup>2</sup>, then what is the difference between unit digit of A and B?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 4<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + .... + 44<sup>3 </sup>&#2324;&#2352; B = 12<sup>2</sup> + 18<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup> + .... + 54<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2", "0", "4", "3"], "options_hi": ["2", "0", "4", "3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>A = 4<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + .... + 44<sup>3</sup></p><p>A = 64 * (1<sup>3 </sup>+ 2<sup>3</sup> +3<sup>3</sup> + ... + 11<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>Here, we know that, (1<sup>3 </sup>+ 2<sup>3</sup> + 3<sup>3</sup> + ... + n<sup>3</sup>) = (n(n + 1)/2)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Then, A = 64 * ((11(11 + 1)/2)<sup>2</sup>) = 278784</p><p>Unit digit of A = 4</p><p>Similarly, B = 12<sup>2</sup> + 18<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup> + .... + 54<sup>2</sup></p><p>B = 36 * ((2<sup>2 </sup>+ 3<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> + ... + 9<sup>2</sup>)  -  1<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here, we know that, (1<sup>2 </sup>+ 2<sup>2</sup> + 3<sup>2</sup> + ... + n<sup>2</sup>) = n(n + 1)(2n + 1)/6</p><p>Then, B = 36 * ((9(9 + 1)(18 + 1)/6)  -  1) = 10224</p><p>Unit digit of B = 4</p><p>Therefore, difference between unit digit of A and B = 4  -  4 = <b>0</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A = 4<sup>3</sup> + 8<sup>3</sup> + 12<sup>3</sup> + .... + 44<sup>3</sup></p><p>A = 64 * (1<sup>3 </sup>+ 2<sup>3</sup> +3<sup>3</sup> + ... + 11<sup>3</sup>)</p><p>Here, we know that, (1<sup>3 </sup>+ 2<sup>3</sup> + 3<sup>3</sup> + ... + n<sup>3</sup>) = (n(n + 1)/2)<sup>2</sup></p><p>Then, A = 64 * ((11(11 + 1)/2)<sup>2</sup>) = 278784</p><p>Unit digit of A = 4</p><p>Similarly, B = 12<sup>2</sup> + 18<sup>2</sup> + 24<sup>2</sup> + .... + 54<sup>2</sup></p><p>B = 36 * ((2<sup>2 </sup>+ 3<sup>2</sup> + 4<sup>2</sup> + ... + 9<sup>2</sup>)  -  1<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>Here, we know that, (1<sup>2 </sup>+ 2<sup>2</sup> + 3<sup>2</sup> + ... + n<sup>2</sup>) = n(n + 1)(2n + 1)/6</p><p>Then, B = 36 * ((9(9 + 1)(18 + 1)/6)  -  1) = 10224</p><p>Unit digit of B = 4</p><p>Therefore, difference between unit digit of A and B = 4  -  4 = <b>0</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Out of the fractions 3/5, 5/7, 7/8, 8/9, which is the third smallest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; 3/5, 5/7, 7/8, 8/9 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3/5", "7/8", "8/9", "5/7"], "options_hi": ["3/5", "7/8", "8/9", "5/7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If population of State B in 2002 was 20 lakhs, what will be the average population of the state in 2003 and 2004?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 2002 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 20 &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2341;&#2368;, 2003 &#2324;&#2352; 2004 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["3250000", "2930000", "3430000", "3140000"], "options_hi": ["3250000", "2930000", "3430000", "3140000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Population State B in 2003 = 20x1.4 = 28 lakhs</p> <p>Population State B in 2004 = 28x1.45 = 40.6 lakhs</p> <p>Average population = (28+40.6)/2 = 34.3 lakhs</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Population State B in 2003 = 20x1.4 = 28 lakhs</p> <p>Population State B in 2004 = 28x1.45 = 40.6 lakhs</p> <p>Average population = (28+40.6)/2 = 34.3 lakhs</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following bar graph shows the number of students of two teams in four different schools.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=Image1 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24667/image009.gif\"></p><p>Find the average of the number of students in School A, School C, School D, and School B of Team B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2335;&#2368;&#2350;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Image1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24667/image009.gif\"></p><p>&#2335;&#2368;&#2350; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; A, &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; C, &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; D &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["415", "435", "445", "425"], "options_hi": ["415", "435", "445", "425"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of students in team B of School A = 440</p><p>Number of students in team B of School B = 420</p><p>Number of students in team B of School C = 480</p><p>Number of students in team B of School D = 400</p><p>Required average = (440 + 420 + 480 + 400)/4 = 435</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of students in team B of School A = 440</p><p>Number of students in team B of School B = 420</p><p>Number of students in team B of School C = 480</p><p>Number of students in team B of School D = 400</p><p>Required average = (440 + 420 + 480 + 400)/4 = 435</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If sum of n consecutive positive even numbers is 2352, find n.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 2352 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; n &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["46", "48", "51", "49"], "options_hi": ["46", "48", "51", "49"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of n consecutive even numbers = n(n+1) = 2352</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>+ n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> + 49n  -  48n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n = -49 or +48</p><p>Hence, n = <b>48</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of n consecutive even numbers = n(n+1) = 2352</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>+ n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n<sup>2</sup> + 49n  -  48n  -  2352 = 0</p><p>n = -49 or +48</p><p>Hence, n = <b>48</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>ABCDEF is a six digit number such that digit A = digit D, digit B = digit E and digit C = digit F. So, ABCDEF is always divisible by:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>ABCDEF &#2331;&#2361; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; A = &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; D, &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; B = &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; E &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; C = &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; F &#2311;&#2360;&#2354;&#2367;&#2319; ABCDEF &#2360;&#2342;&#2376;&#2357; ____ &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["111", "1001", "19", "101"], "options_hi": ["111", "1001", "19", "101"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p>ABCDEF = ABCABC</p><p>We know that any six-digit number that is formed by repeating a three-digit number, is always divisible by 1001.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p>ABCDEF = ABCABC</p><p>We know that any six-digit number that is formed by repeating a three-digit number, is always divisible by 1001.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a school, 30% are boys and rest are girls. If 60% of boys and 80% of girls are present on a certain day, then find the percentage of students absent on that day.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; 60% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 80% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2313;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["15%", "30%", "26%", "18%"], "options_hi": ["15%", "30%", "26%", "18%"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of students in the school = 100</p><p>Number of boys in the school = 30</p><p>Number of girls in the school = 70</p><p>Total number of absent students = (100 - 60)% of 30 + (100  -  80)% of 70</p><p>= 12 + 14</p><p>= 26</p><p>Hence, percentage of students absent on that day = 26%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of students in the school = 100</p><p>Number of boys in the school = 30</p><p>Number of girls in the school = 70</p><p>Total number of absent students = (100 - 60)% of 30 + (100  -  80)% of 70</p><p>= 12 + 14</p><p>= 26</p><p>Hence, percentage of students absent on that day = 26%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The fraction 22.5/100000 in decimal form is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 22.5/100000 &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["0.00225", "0.000225", "0.0000225", "0.0225"], "options_hi": ["0.00225", "0.000225", "0.0000225", "0.0225"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=124 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image001.png\"></p><p>= 5 + (32  -  3)/90  -  3  -  (25  -  2)/90 + 2 + (21  -  2)/90</p><p>= 4 + 29/90  -  23/90 + 19/90</p><p>= 385/90 = 77/18</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}]}